00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:13.792
who up here, amongst us,
is the coolest onstage?

00:03:13.792 --> 00:03:14.750
Who's the most nervous?

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:17.180
Who's anxious being on
stage in front of everyone?

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:20.940
So there's one really reliable
way to detect stress in humans.

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:23.024
It's a chemical called cortisol.

00:03:23.024 --> 00:03:24.440
You can test for
it in your blood.

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:25.981
And its presence
and the amount of it

00:03:25.981 --> 00:03:28.101
tells you empirically
how stressed out you are.

00:03:28.101 --> 00:03:29.600
I asked the organizers,
and they did

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:30.974
tell me I'm not
allowed to create

00:03:30.974 --> 00:03:32.510
a biohazard situation on stage.

00:03:32.510 --> 00:03:34.320
So I couldn't do blood testing.

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:36.960
So the next step, what
about blood pressure?

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:38.660
So blood pressure,
how elevated it is,

00:03:38.660 --> 00:03:40.310
will tell you how
stressed you are.

00:03:40.310 --> 00:03:42.780
Let's think about a
blood pressure cuff.

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:45.150
It requires that you can
detect your heart rate,

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:47.460
and you have to be able to
apply and release pressure

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.590
in an even way around your arm.

00:03:49.590 --> 00:03:52.410
It's totally doable with IoT,
but maybe a little ambitious

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:53.910
for a 50 minute session.

00:03:53.910 --> 00:03:55.690
So I kind of got rid of that.

00:03:55.690 --> 00:03:57.510
So our last option
that I fell back to

00:03:57.510 --> 00:04:00.970
is this thing called
the vagal tone impulse.

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:02.160
This is your vagus nerve.

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:04.440
The vagus nerve is what
regulates your heart rate.

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:07.830
It's what keeps your heart
rate within normal amounts.

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:10.580
During times of extreme
stress, the vagal tone impulse

00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:13.110
is suppressed, so that your
heart rate can skyrocket,

00:04:13.110 --> 00:04:15.694
so that you can be ready
to do whatever you want.

00:04:15.694 --> 00:04:17.610
The comment-- you've
probably heard about it--

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:19.240
is the fight or flight response.

00:04:19.240 --> 00:04:21.073
So once you're in that
mode, your heart rate

00:04:21.073 --> 00:04:24.954
can go up, even though you don't
have any physical need for it.

00:04:24.954 --> 00:04:26.370
So for example,
if you're nervous,

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:28.770
and you want to tear
off stage and run away,

00:04:28.770 --> 00:04:32.009
you'll get your body
flooded with blood

00:04:32.009 --> 00:04:33.300
so that you can do that faster.

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:35.092
So why am I giving you
this biology lesson?

00:04:35.092 --> 00:04:36.591
I could have just
said, hey, we want

00:04:36.591 --> 00:04:38.670
to know who's nervous on
stage, and away we go.

