00:33:50.236 --> 00:33:51.530
app doing the data pulling.

00:33:51.530 --> 00:33:52.785
So go ahead, Rob.

00:33:52.785 --> 00:33:54.090
ROB WORMALD: OK.

00:33:54.090 --> 00:33:55.570
Switch over to my editor.

00:33:55.570 --> 00:33:56.850
So I'm using Angular.

00:33:56.850 --> 00:33:59.220
And obviously, I used the
Angular CLI to go ahead

00:33:59.220 --> 00:34:00.750
and scaffold a
project, so it set up

00:34:00.750 --> 00:34:02.666
tooling and building and
all that stuff that's

00:34:02.666 --> 00:34:03.875
really hard about JavaScript.

00:34:03.875 --> 00:34:05.540
I started-- the first
thing we looked at

00:34:05.540 --> 00:34:06.630
was our devices screen.

00:34:06.630 --> 00:34:08.130
And that's just a
couple of screens.

00:34:08.130 --> 00:34:09.870
So I've got a very
simple device list

00:34:09.870 --> 00:34:13.039
component, a little bit of HTML
with some Angular bindings.

00:34:13.039 --> 00:34:14.580
We're just iterating
over our devices

00:34:14.580 --> 00:34:15.855
and rendering some data.

00:34:15.855 --> 00:34:17.355
One of the nice
things about Angular

00:34:17.355 --> 00:34:19.438
is that we have a really,
really good relationship

00:34:19.438 --> 00:34:20.159
with Firebase.

00:34:20.159 --> 00:34:22.679
So we have a really nice
built in Firebase Angular

00:34:22.679 --> 00:34:24.030
library, Angular Firestore.

00:34:24.030 --> 00:34:26.280
And so it takes one line of
code to talk to Firestore,

00:34:26.280 --> 00:34:28.139
extract that data,
and then I get

00:34:28.139 --> 00:34:30.219
a real time display of that.

00:34:30.219 --> 00:34:32.764
We go a little more in depth
into our detailed view.

00:34:32.764 --> 00:34:34.389
You can see we're
doing the same thing.

00:34:34.389 --> 00:34:36.513
We're just using our built
in Angular Fire service.

00:34:36.513 --> 00:34:38.348
We are just extracting
data, getting

00:34:38.348 --> 00:34:40.139
some routing parameters,
and just streaming

00:34:40.139 --> 00:34:42.570
the last measurements
off of the device.

00:34:42.570 --> 00:34:44.429
So that's kind of basic
Angular templating.

00:34:44.429 --> 00:34:45.672
That works pretty simply.

00:34:45.672 --> 00:34:48.130
For the pulse graph, because
that's a lot more complicated,

00:34:48.130 --> 00:34:50.040
we're using D-3, which
is an awesome graphing

00:34:50.040 --> 00:34:51.630
library that's open source.

00:34:51.630 --> 00:34:53.250
Again, we're just
talking to Firebase,

00:34:53.250 --> 00:34:54.814
getting that device
data coming out.

00:34:54.814 --> 00:34:56.230
I won't bore you
